    {
      "id": 181,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2040,
        5080
      ],
      "size": [
        880,
        440
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 36,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Guide: ReCaVSR One-Step Streaming Video Super-Resolution (R2V)",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# ReCaVSR One-Step Streaming Super-Resolution (R2V)\n**Powered by Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B + FlashDecoder (`PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-ReCaVSR`)**\n\n### 1. Stage 1: 768p Draft Video Generation\n- Generates and saves the playable 768p draft video in **Save Video (Stage 1)** first.\n\n### 2. Interactive Approval Gate (Zero Timer — No `Ctrl+M` Needed!)\n- As soon as the 768p draft finishes, execution pauses indefinitely at **⚡ Stage 1 -> Stage 2 Approval Gate (Node #169)**.\n- Watch the 768p video right in the UI, then click one of the interactive buttons (either on the top floating bar or on Node #169):\n  - **✅ Approve & Upscale (2x / 2K)**: Runs ReCaVSR at **2.0x** scale (e.g., 768p → 1536p / 2K).\n  - **🚀 Approve & Upscale (4x / 4K)**: Runs ReCaVSR at **4.0x** scale (e.g., 768p → 3072p / 4K).\n  - **🛑 Stop Here (Keep 768p Only)**: Stops immediately without running the upscaler!\n- You can also change `approval_mode` on Node #169 to `Auto-Upscale Immediately` or `Stop After 768p Draft Only`, and set the default `upscale_factor` (`2x` vs `4x`).\n\n### 3. ReCaVSR Settings (Node #171)\n- **Model**: `transformer_int8_convrot.safetensors` (1.8x faster, 4 GB less VRAM) or `transformer.safetensors` (BF16).\n- **Decoder**: `flashdecoder` (streams block-by-block in 8–10 GB VRAM and preserves audio & frame rate automatically).\n- **Color Fix**: `wavelet` (preserves exact Stage 1 color grading while restoring high-frequency detail).\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
